A Go target in a build that becomes a binary declares package main whatever
package its output block names: Go links func main() nowhere else. With the
named package kept, `sngl run` built an archive and failed exec'ing it with
"permission denied". The golden is the runnable build, so it shows package
main; `sngl generate` keeps the named package
(cmd/sngl/testdata/generate_go_main_keeps_package.txt).

deny * `package widgets` -- an executable build links main() only in package main
-- main.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        gtk4(gir="builtin", package="widgets", main=true)
        fyne(package="widgets", main=true)
        bubbletea(package="widgets", main=true)
    }
}

ui.window #app(title="Hi") {
    ui.text(value="hi")
}
